---
// The artifact card: one owner's complete take, laid out like a model card but
// about an intervention rather than a model.
//
// Body carries the author's own words, which is what makes a disagreement between
// two submissions interpretable rather than just a number gap. The rail carries
// the application contract, because a vector downloaded without it gets applied
// wrong and then appears not to work.
import SweepChart from "./SweepChart.astro";
import ConfoundChart from "./ConfoundChart.astro";
import AbsenceReason from "./AbsenceReason.astro";

interface Props {
  claimant: any;
  modelId: string;
}
const { claimant: c, modelId } = Astro.props;
const fmt = (v) => (v === null || v === undefined ? null : v.toFixed(4));
const r = c.recipe;

// Why a field has no value, in the author's words. Empty for almost every
// submission and that is the ordinary state: an absence with nobody's account
// of it renders as it always did, and a missing reason is not a finding.
const absences = c.absences ?? {};

// Which of them this card already prints beside the field itself. A layout
// fact about this card, not a list of the fields allowed a reason: the schema
// puts no set on the field name, so anything not named here still has to reach
// the reader rather than being silently dropped. `elsewhere` is how.
const beside = [
  "model_revision", "chat_template_hash", "steering_position",
  "coeff_low", "coeff_high", "l2_norm", "activation_norm", "license_status",
  "shape", "dtype",
];
const elsewhere = Object.entries(absences).filter(([f]) => !beside.includes(f));
---

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-main">
    <h2>Definition</h2>
    <p class="definition" data-authored>{c.definition}</p>

    <h2>Method</h2>
    {r ? (
      <>
        <p class="provenance">
          Profile <span class="mono">{r.profile}</span>, namespaced and versioned.
          Not chosen from a list, because there is no list.
        </p>
        <dl class="spec">
          {Object.entries(r.payload).map(([k, v]) => (
            <>
              <dt>{k.replace(/_/g, " ")}</dt>
              <dd>{String(v)}</dd>
            </>
          ))}
        </dl>

        <h2>Author's theory</h2>
        <p class="definition" data-authored>{r.theory}</p>

        <h2>Reproducing it</h2>
        <dl class="spec">
          <dt>entrypoint</dt>
          <dd class="mono">
            {r.entrypoint_library
              ? [r.entrypoint_library, r.entrypoint_version].filter(Boolean).join(" ")
              : "not recorded"}
          </dd>
          <dt>container</dt>
          <dd class="mono">{r.container_digest ?? "not recorded"}</dd>
        </dl>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p class="note absent-block">
        No recipe. This artifact was published without a reproducible procedure,
        which is a valid submission: a vector from a paper with no runnable code is
        worth holding, and requiring a recipe would exclude exactly the historical
        artifacts worth comparing against. It does mean nobody can rerun this one,
        and the only thing distinguishing it from a behaviourally equivalent vector
        is the label on it.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>Evidence</h2>
    <div class="measures">
      <div>
        <span class="k">Trait score</span>
        {c.score_state === "reportable" && fmt(c.trait_score)}
        {c.score_state === "uninterpretable" && (
          <span class="uninterpretable">uninterpretable</span>
        )}
        {c.score_state === "absent" && <span class="absent">not measured</span>}
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="k">Coherence</span>
        {c.coherence_score === null
          ? <span class="absent">not measured</span>
          : fmt(c.coherence_score)}
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="k">Transfer</span>
        {c.transfer_score === null
          ? <span class="absent">not measured</span>
          : fmt(c.transfer_score)}
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="k">Confound axes checked</span>
        {c.axes.length ? c.axes.join(", ") : <span class="absent">none declared</span>}
      </div>
    </div>

    {c.score_state === "uninterpretable" && (
      <p class="note">
        A trait score was reported with no coherence measure beside it, so it shows
        as uninterpretable rather than as a number. Judge agreement collapses on
        degenerate text, which makes an unpaired score a broken instrument rather
        than a small effect.
      </p>
    )}

    {c.notes && <p class="note">{c.notes}</p>}

    <h2>Coefficient sweep</h2>
    <SweepChart curve={c.coeff_curve} synthetic={c.is_synthetic} />

    <h2>Trait against its collateral axes</h2>
    <ConfoundChart
      trait={c.trait_score}
      coherence={c.coherence_score}
      confounds={c.confounds}
      traitState={c.score_state}
      synthetic={c.is_synthetic}
    />

  </div>

  <aside class="card-rail">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Application contract</h3>
      <dl class="spec tight">
        <dt>kind</dt><dd class="mono">{c.kind}</dd>
        <dt>model</dt>
        <dd><a class="mono" href={`/models/${modelId}/`}>{modelId}</a></dd>
        <dt>revision</dt>
        <dd class="mono">
          {c.model_revision ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="model_revision" />
        </dd>
        <dt>layer</dt><dd>{c.layer} <span class="meta">{c.layer_convention}</span></dd>
        <dt>hook point</dt><dd class="mono">{c.hook_point}</dd>
        <dt>chat template</dt>
        <dd class="mono">
          {c.chat_template_hash ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="chat_template_hash" />
        </dd>
        <dt>steering position</dt>
        <dd>
          {c.steering_position ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="steering_position" />
        </dd>
        <dt>coefficient</dt>
        <dd>
          {c.coeff_low === null
            ? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>
            : `${c.coeff_low} to ${c.coeff_high}`}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="coeff_low" />
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="coeff_high" />
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="why">
        A vector applied at the wrong layer, hook point or chat template appears
        not to work rather than failing loudly. That is why this sits beside the
        artifact and not in a README.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Tensor</h3>
      <dl class="spec tight">
        <dt>shape</dt>
        <dd class="mono">
          {c.shape}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="shape" />
        </dd>
        <dt>dtype</dt>
        <dd class="mono">
          {c.dtype}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="dtype" />
        </dd>
        <dt>L2 norm</dt>
        <dd>
          {c.l2_norm ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="l2_norm" />
        </dd>
        <dt>activation norm</dt>
        <dd>
          {c.activation_norm ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <span class="meta">at that layer</span>
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="activation_norm" />
        </dd>
        <dt>format</dt><dd class="mono">safetensors</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="why">
        Activation norm is here so a coefficient can be a fraction of activation
        magnitude rather than a raw alpha, which means nothing across models.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Distribution</h3>
      <dl class="spec tight">
        <dt>license status</dt>
        <dd>
          {c.license_status === "unresolved"
            ? <span class="uninterpretable">unresolved</span>
            : c.license_status ?? <span class="absent">not recorded</span>}
          <AbsenceReason reasons={absences} field="license_status" />
        </dd>
        <dt>downloads</dt><dd><span class="absent">not tracked</span></dd>
        <dt>stars</dt><dd><span class="absent">not tracked</span></dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="why">
        A steering vector is derived from model weights, so redistribution may be
        constrained by the source model's license. Unresolved means nobody has
        checked, and an artifact whose rights are unresolved cannot be served.
      </p>
    </div>

    {elsewhere.length > 0 && (
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Also accounted for</h3>
        <dl class="spec tight">
          {elsewhere.map(([field, reason]) => (
            <>
              <dt class="mono">{field}</dt>
              <dd><span class="absence-reason" data-authored>{reason}</span></dd>
            </>
          ))}
        </dl>
        <p class="why">
          Absences about fields this card has no line for. The schema puts no set
          on which field a reason may be about, so there is nowhere to drop one
          quietly: anything not printed beside its own field lands here.
        </p>
      </div>
    )}
  </aside>
</div>
